=== PARITY (vs web HttpStatusTool.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (HttpStatusSource → HttpStatusModel): the web tool
    reads the HTTP_CODES *module constant* + useTranslation (no async hook). The native StaticHttpStatusSource
    serves HttpStatusCatalog (the verbatim catalog port) immediately, exactly as the web module imports the
    constant; the seam still models loading/empty/error/freshness so every state renders. NO HTTP in the view.
  Projection → HttpStatusProjector is a 1:1 port of the web derivations:
    • filter = the `filtered` useMemo — `if (!search.trim()) return all`, else `q = search.toLowerCase()`
      (untrimmed) and `String(code).includes(q) || text.toLowerCase().includes(q) ||
      desc.toLowerCase().includes(q)`. The untrimmed-lowercase nuance (`' 40'` → ∅) is unit-asserted.
    • tone = the Badge variant ternary `code<300 success : <400 info : <500 warning : danger`.
    • sort = the DataTable `sortable` code column (tri-state unsorted→asc→desc numeric compare).
    • pagination = DataTable `pagination` (defaultPageSize 25 → the 19 rows fit one page; bar shows range).
    Verified by an EXECUTED harness (55/55).
  Composition → web ToolCard (GlassPanel + amber IconBox + title `Http Status` + desc `Http Status Desc`) →
    TSGlassPanel + TSIconBox(network, .warning) + title/desc. Body: search Input (leading Network icon) →
    HttpStatusSearchField; DataTable (code badge / status text / status desc, sortable header, pagination) →
    HttpStatusColumnHeader + HttpStatusRowView + HttpStatusPaginationBar.
  Shared components → maps web @/components/ui to native: Badge→HttpStatusBadge, Input→HttpStatusSearchField,
    DataTable→local header+rows+pagination, GlassPanel→TSGlassPanel, IconBox→TSIconBox, Skeleton→TSSkeleton,
    EmptyState→ContentUnavailableView. The badge/field/rows are authored locally over the SAME P1/S9 tokens
    as the shared TSBadge/TSTextField so every label resolves through the per-surface HttpStatusStrings table
    (the shared components take only a LocalizedStringKey) — identical rationale to the sibling widgets.
    Recharts→none / Leaflet→none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton table) · empty (catalog has no rows → ContentUnavailableView +
    retry) · error (icon + message + retry) · content · search-empty (in-table ContentUnavailableView, search
    field stays visible) · stale/offline (freshness chip over cached rows). Model phase resolution keeps
    cached rows visible behind background refresh/errors; a hard failure with no cache → error.
  i18n → all six web keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade. They are natural-language phrases ABSENT from
    web en.json, so i18next renders them verbatim (`t('Http Status')` → "Http Status"); the native fallbacks
    reproduce that exactly (cross-checked: 0 missing keys; plutil -lint OK). No English literals in native
    code (every Text routes through HttpStatusStrings / .text).
  a11y → badge carries "{code} {class}" (the HTTP class is added as words so the badge color is not the only
    signal); rows carry a combined "{code} {class}. {text}. {desc}" label; search field, sortable header,
    refresh/retry and pagination buttons all have accessibilityLabels (+ sort hint); the table exposes
    accessibilityValue = HttpStatusAccessibility.summary. Dynamic Type via Font.TS tokens; Reduce Motion
    honored by the shared TSSkeleton shimmer.
  Telemetry → HttpStatusModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"HttpStatusTool") → bridges the shared
    Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test + the executed model wiring.

